<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  What the release is allowed to do beyond the hardened runtime's defaults (build.sh release signs with it).
  The hardened runtime blocks the microphone unless it's asked for here, so this is the one thing Koe needs:

  com.apple.security.device.audio-input — record the microphone. macOS still asks the person first
      (NSMicrophoneUsageDescription in Info.plist).

  Not needed, so not here:
  - system audio (other apps' sound): Core Audio process taps have no entitlement; macOS asks the person
    (NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription in Info.plist);
  - the network (speech models, update checks): only sandboxed apps need com.apple.security.network.client,
    and Koe isn't sandboxed (it isn't on the Mac App Store);
  - JIT, unsigned memory, DYLD variables: the speech models run through Core ML.

  Added by build.sh only to an ad-hoc signed release (no Developer ID certificate), never to this file:
  com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation — the hardened runtime loads only libraries signed by the
      same team as the app, and an ad-hoc signature has no team, so without it the app can't load its own
      Sparkle.framework. With a Developer ID the app and the framework share a team and it isn't needed.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key><true/>
</dict>
</plist>
